18 0 obj
<< /A 67 0 R /Alt (Infographic illustration of a fighter pilot in a cockpit, surrounded by labels identifying psychophysiological stressors in advanced fighter aviation, including acceleration \(+Gz\) loading, hypoxia, prolonged sorties, spatial disorientation, cognitive workload, helmet-mounted display risks, sensor fusion, acoustic and thermal stress, cardiovascular strain, and neurological strain, emphasizing demands on central nervous system resilience.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 68 0 R /Alt (Infographic explains autonomic regulation, heart rate variability, and allostatic load in military aviators, highlighting the autonomic nervous system, stressors in aviation, HRV metrics, effects of sustained stress, allostatic load risks, and benefits of continuous monitoring using wearables.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 69 0 R /Alt (Infographic illustrating how high-G acceleration, hypoxia, and hypobaric decompression in fighter pilots may contribute to brain and vascular changes, including microbubbles and venous gas emboli, oxidative stress, inflammatory dysregulation, altered blood-brain barrier permeability, neurovascular dysfunction, glymphatic impairment, and reduced metabolic waste removal.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 70 0 R /Alt (Infographic illustrating wearable biosensors for near-continuous aerospace health monitoring, with four sections: wearable sensing platforms, remote monitoring, analytics with AI/ML for readiness, and operational applications, supported by implementation requirements for optimized health, performance, and resilience.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 52 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 71 0 R /Alt (Infographic detailing longitudinal psychophysiological monitoring in fighter pilots across four phases: legacy airframe, conversion training, next-generation operations, and career-span monitoring. Each phase outlines objectives such as establishing baseline profiles, quantifying adaptation and stress, monitoring cumulative operational load, and modeling resilience or vulnerability. Illustrations include different aircraft and a saluting pilot. A graph below shows trajectories of autonomic balance, cognitive load, sensory strain, and neural stress markers over time, highlighting individualized baseline, adaptation, recovery, resilience, and vulnerability paths. Integrates AI and machine learning for early intervention and optimization of pilot health, performance, and readiness.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 55 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
